      "id": 10386,
      "name": "ronicus",
      "username": "ronicus",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/cdc98d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-27T18:37:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello,</p><p>Is there a difference between \"Destroyed\" versus \"Discarded\"?&nbsp; My thought was that \"Destroy\" means to put out-of-play (i.e. no longer able to be used for that match) and \"Discard\" means put it in the appropriate discard pile for potential re-circulation and/or selection based on card ability.&nbsp; The issue came up with regards to Expatriette.&nbsp; When her \"ammo\" cards are used, the are \"Destroyed\" (which would make sense because it's ammo).&nbsp; This would mean that she *never* gets them back for that session (limited amount of ammo, for example).</p><p>Is this correct?&nbsp; Or, do \"Destroy\" and \"Discard\" *both* go back to the appropriate discard piel for potential re-circulation and/or selection based on card ability?</p><p>Thanks in advance!</p><p>-Ronicus</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:25.319Z",
