      "raw": "<p>Hello,</p><p>Is there a difference between &quot;Destroyed&quot; versus &quot;Discarded&quot;?&nbsp; My thought was that &quot;Destroy&quot; means to put out-of-play (i.e. no longer able to be used for that match) and &quot;Discard&quot; means put it in the appropriate discard pile for potential re-circulation and/or selection based on card ability.&nbsp; The issue came up with regards to Expatriette.&nbsp; When her &quot;ammo&quot; cards are used, the are &quot;Destroyed&quot; (which would make sense because it&#39;s ammo).&nbsp; This would mean that she *never* gets them back for that session (limited amount of ammo, for example).</p><p>Is this correct?&nbsp; Or, do &quot;Destroy&quot; and &quot;Discard&quot; *both* go back to the appropriate discard piel for potential re-circulation and/or selection based on card ability?</p><p>Thanks in advance!</p><p>-Ronicus</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
