      "created_at": "2014-07-26T20:17:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Discard is from cards that are not in play. If an effect says to discard cards without clarification, it means from your hand; if it specifies that you must discard from the top of your deck, from revealed cards, et cetera, then of course you discard from there. Only cards in play can be destroyed.</p><p>That seems to cover everything.</p>",
